## 🧪 Simulation Output

The 4-bit shift register was simulated using a Verilog testbench. The testbench applies a reset signal and then shifts the serial input data into the register on each rising edge of the clock.

### Input Sequence

```text
Serial Input: 1 → 0 → 1 → 1
```

### Expected Output

| Clock Cycle | Reset | Serial Input | `Q[3:0]` |
| ----------: | ----: | -----------: | -------: |
|           0 |     1 |            0 |   `0000` |
|           1 |     0 |            1 |   `0001` |
|           2 |     0 |            0 |   `0010` |
|           3 |     0 |            1 |   `0101` |
|           4 |     0 |            1 |   `1011` |

